/* Eager (above-the-fold) homepage thumbnails: load straight from HTML (no JS gate).
   width/height attrs reserve the aspect ratio so there's no layout shift; dark bg
   while the image decodes, matching the lazy .thumb box. Added 2026-07-15. */
.gallery .cover .thumb > img.thumb-eager{
  display:block; width:100%; height:auto; margin:0;
  border-radius:5px 5px 0 0; background:#1a1a1a;
}
/* Eager thumbs carry no .lazyload class, so the generic
   `.thumb:not(:has(> img.lazyload))::before{display:none}` rule above was killing their
   spinner outright — the first (most visible) row had NO loading indicator, it just popped
   in. Show the spinner while an eager image is still downloading; the inline onload adds
   .is-loaded the moment it decodes, which hides it again. The spinner is a positioned
   ::before painting over the static <img>, so it MUST be hidden on load or it would sit on
   top of the finished image. onerror also adds .is-loaded once fallbacks are exhausted, so a
   permanently broken thumb stops spinning instead of hanging forever. Added 2026-07-16. */
.gallery .cover .thumb:has(> img.thumb-eager)::before{ display:block; }
.gallery .cover .thumb:has(> img.thumb-eager.is-loaded)::before{ display:none; }
